Course.start({"num":7,"unit":2,"slug":"m07-articulos","minutes":40,"title":"Los artículos","subtitle":"Definite and indefinite articles: el, la, los, las, un, una, unos, unas","lede":"English has *the* and *a*. Spanish has eight words for them, because the article has to match its noun. Spanish also uses *the* in places where English doesn't.","recap":"Last time you learned that every noun is masculine or feminine, how to tell from its ending, and how to make nouns plural.","context":{"title":"Un templo sin terminar","place":"Barcelona, España","text":"In **1882**, workers in Barcelona began building a church called **la Sagrada Família** (the Holy Family). A year later, a young architect named **Antoni Gaudí** took over the project. He designed towers that look like they grew from the ground, columns shaped like trees, and windows that fill the inside with colored light.\n\nGaudí worked on it for over 40 years, until his death in 1926. When people asked him why it was taking so long, he is said to have answered, \"My client is not in a hurry.\" More than 140 years after it began, construction still continues, paid for by visitors and donations.\n\nListen to how people describe it: {{la Sagrada Família es una iglesia}}. The word **la** means *the* (this one specific church). **Una** means *a* (one of many churches). Choosing between them is what this module is about."},"learn":[{"title":"*The*: el, la, los, las","text":"The **definite article** points to something specific. It has four forms to match the noun's gender and number.","table":{"head":["","Singular","Plural"],"rows":[["Masculine","{{el libro}}","{{los libros}}"],["Feminine","{{la mochila}}","{{las mochilas}}"]]}},{"title":"*A, an, some*: un, una, unos, unas","text":"The **indefinite article** talks about something that isn't specific: *a* book, *some* pencils.","table":{"head":["","Singular","Plural"],"rows":[["Masculine","{{un cuaderno}} (a notebook)","{{unos cuadernos}} (some notebooks)"],["Feminine","{{una carpeta}} (a folder)","{{unas carpetas}} (some folders)"]]},"flash":[["el cuaderno","notebook"],["la mochila","backpack"],["el bolígrafo","pen"],["el lápiz","pencil"],["la calculadora","calculator"],["la carpeta","folder"],["la regla","ruler"],["el diccionario","dictionary"],["la computadora","computer (Latin America)"],["el ordenador","computer (Spain)"]]},{"title":"When Spanish uses *the* and English doesn't","text":"Spanish uses **el, la, los, las** in a few places where English uses nothing at all:\n- **Talking about things in general:** {{La música es importante.}} (*Music is important.*) · {{Me gusta el chocolate.}} (*I like chocolate.*)\n- **Titles, when you talk *about* someone:** {{El señor Ruiz es mi profesor.}} But when you talk *to* them, no article: {{Buenos días, señor Ruiz.}}\n- **Days of the week**, for *on*: {{Tengo examen el viernes.}} (*I have a test on Friday.*)\n\nAnd Spanish leaves out *a* with jobs and identities after *ser* (*to be*): {{Ella es profesora.}} (*She's a teacher.*) {{Soy estudiante.}} (*I'm a student.*)","tip":"Words like *agua* are feminine, but they start with a stressed **a** sound, so they use **el** and **un** in the singular: {{el agua}}, {{un águila}} (an eagle). The plural is normal: {{las aguas}}."}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"select","title":"Choose *the*","intro":"Choose the definite article that matches each noun.","items":[{"s":"{el|la|los|las} cuaderno"},{"s":"{las|los|la|el} mochilas"},{"s":"{los|las|el|la} lápices"},{"s":"{la|el|las|los} calculadora"},{"s":"{el|la|los|las} mapa","why":"*Mapa* is an exception: masculine."},{"s":"{las|los|la|el} canciones"},{"s":"{los|las|el|la} días"},{"s":"{la|el|las|los} mano","why":"*Mano* is an exception: feminine."}],"hints":["Two questions: masculine or feminine? Singular or plural?","Remember the exceptions: *el mapa, el día, la mano*."]},{"id":"t2","type":"cloze","title":"Write *a* or *some*","intro":"Write **un**, **una**, **unos** or **unas**.","items":["Necesito [un] cuaderno.","Hay [una] mochila en la silla.","Compro [unos] bolígrafos.","Tengo [unas] carpetas nuevas.","Hay [un] mapa en la pared.","Juan tiene [una] foto de su perro.","Necesitamos [unos] lápices.","Hay [unas] calculadoras en la mesa."],"hints":["Masculine: **un** / **unos**. Feminine: **una** / **unas**.","*Foto* is feminine (short for *fotografía*). *Mapa* is masculine."]},{"id":"t3","type":"match","title":"En la clase","intro":"Tap a Spanish word (you'll hear it), then its meaning.","pairs":[["el cuaderno","notebook"],["la mochila","backpack"],["el bolígrafo","pen"],["la regla","ruler"],["la carpeta","folder"],["la silla","chair"],["la pizarra","board"],["la ventana","window"],["la puerta","door"]],"hints":["*Ventana* sounds a little like *ventilation*: a window."]},{"id":"t4","type":"listen","title":"The, a or some?","intro":"Listen and choose the meaning.","questions":[{"say":"un libro","choices":[["a book",true],["the book",false],["some books",false],["the books",false]]},{"say":"las mesas","choices":[["the tables",true],["a table",false],["some tables",false],["the table",false]]},{"say":"unas sillas","choices":[["some chairs",true],["the chairs",false],["a chair",false],["the chair",false]]},{"say":"la ventana","choices":[["the window",true],["a window",false],["the windows",false],["some windows",false]]},{"say":"unos bolígrafos","choices":[["some pens",true],["the pens",false],["a pen",false],["the pen",false]]}],"hints":["Words that start with **u** (*un, una, unos, unas*) mean *a* or *some*.","Words with **l** (*el, la, los, las*) mean *the*."]},{"id":"t5","type":"errors","title":"Fix the article","intro":"Each sentence has one wrong article. Tap it, then type the right one.","items":[{"s":"Necesito el lápices.","bad":"el","fix":"los"},{"s":"Hay unos mochilas en la clase.","bad":"unos","fix":"unas"},{"s":"La problema es difícil.","bad":"La","fix":"El","why":"*Problema* is masculine."},{"s":"Tengo un clase de arte.","bad":"un","fix":"una","why":"*Clase* is feminine."},{"s":"Los fotos son bonitas.","bad":"Los","fix":"Las"}],"hints":["Check the noun after each article: gender and number.","Remember: *el problema*, *la clase*, *la foto*."]},{"id":"t6","type":"translate","title":"Spanish uses *the* here","intro":"Translate. Each Spanish sentence needs an article where English has none, or has none where English has *a*.","items":[{"en":"Music is important.","es":["la música es importante"],"why":"General statements need the article: **la música**."},{"en":"Mr. Ruiz is my teacher.","es":["el señor ruiz es mi {profesor|maestro}"],"why":"Talking *about* someone with a title: **el señor**."},{"en":"I have a test on Friday.","es":["[yo] tengo {un examen|una prueba} el viernes"],"why":"*On Friday* = **el viernes**."},{"en":"She's a doctor.","es":["[ella] es {doctora|médica}"],"why":"No *una* with a job after *es*."},{"en":"Water is cold.","es":["el agua está fría","el agua es fría"],"why":"*Agua* uses **el**, but it's feminine: *fría*."}],"hints":["General ideas (*music*, *water*) take **el / la** in Spanish.","Jobs after *es* or *soy* take no article."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say it out loud","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"La Sagrada Família es una iglesia en Barcelona."},{"s":"En mi mochila hay unos cuadernos y un lápiz."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Mi mochila y mi clase","prompt":"Describe what's in your backpack and in your classroom. **Hay** means *there is / there are*. Write **at least 5 sentences**. Use **un / una** at least twice, **unos / unas** at least once, and **el / la / los / las** at least three times.","model":"{{En mi mochila hay un cuaderno y una calculadora.}} {{También hay unos lápices.}} {{El cuaderno es azul.}} {{En la clase hay una pizarra grande.}} {{Las sillas son de madera y la puerta es roja.}}","placeholder":"En mi mochila hay…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 5 sentences","sentences":5},{"t":"**un** or **una** twice","re":"\\b(un|una)\\b","min":2},{"t":"**unos** or **unas**","re":"\\b(unos|unas)\\b"},{"t":"**el, la, los** or **las** three times","re":"\\b(el|la|los|las)\\b","min":3},{"t":"Use **hay**","any":["hay"]}]},"reflect":{"q":"Gaudí knew he would never see the Sagrada Família finished, but he kept working on it for the people who would come after him. What is something you've received from people who came before you (at school, in your family, in your town)? What could you start that someone else might finish?","placeholder":"Something I received from people before me is…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"quiz","title":"Challenge: article puzzles","questions":[{"q":"Which is correct?","choices":[["el agua fría",true,"*Agua* takes **el** but stays feminine: *fría*."],["la agua fría",false],["el agua frío",false],["la agua frío",false]]},{"q":"*Hablo español*, but… which sentence needs an article?","choices":[["___ español es fácil.",true,"When the language is the subject, use **el**: *El español es fácil.*"],["Hablo ___ español.",false],["Estudio ___ español.",false],["¿Hablas ___ inglés?",false]]},{"q":"*Buenos días, ___ señora López.*","choices":[["(nothing)",true,"Talking *to* someone: no article."],["la",false],["una",false],["el",false]]}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** Gaudí also designed **Park Güell** in Barcelona, with a giant mosaic lizard covered in broken pieces of colored tile. This technique is called *trencadís*.","unitTitle":"¿Cómo eres? Sustantivos y descripciones","code":"Mjg4MS1JRFVBRw==","prev":"m06-genero-numero.html","next":"m08-ser.html"});
